# .gitignore — Cloud Expedition Field Journal (learning-azure)
#
# Deny-list tuned for a .NET 10 course whose Learning Mentor integration runs on
# Python 3. Keep this focused: the submodule gitlink (.learning-mentor) and the
# native discovery symlinks (.agents, .claude, .codex, .github) are tracked on
# purpose and must never be ignored.

# --- .NET build output ---------------------------------------------------------
bin/
obj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
x64/
x86/
[Aa][Rr][Mm]/
[Aa][Rr][Mm]64/
artifacts/

# Test + coverage output
[Tt]est[Rr]esult*/
TestResults/
*.trx
*.coverage
*.coveragexml
coverage/
[Cc]overage*/

# MSBuild / build logs
*.binlog
msbuild.*.log
msbuild.log

# --- Visual Studio / Rider / user-specific -------------------------------------
.vs/
*.user
*.suo
*.userprefs
*.rsuser
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# --- Local secrets / environment -----------------------------------------------
# Never commit connection strings, keys, or EULA-accepting env files.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# The one deliberate exception is capstones/*/emulator.env, which is course
# content: it exports Microsoft's published emulator defaults and nothing else,
# and the capstone refuses to start a live run while any of them is set.

# --- Learning Mentor (Python 3) ------------------------------------------------
# The shared state helper and the course-owned adapter both run on Python 3, so
# bytecode caches can appear beside them. Learner progress itself is never stored
# in the repository: the state helper keeps it outside, under
# $XDG_DATA_HOME/learning-mentor/state.sqlite3.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Adapter test fixtures are generated on disk at test time (the runtime forbids
# writing under /tmp), then torn down. Never track them.
.agents/skills/azure-learning-path/tests/.fixtures/

# --- OS cruft ------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
